@page "/evidence"
<SeoHead Title="Evidence and Development Proof"
         Description="Inspect LifeOS milestones, tests, builds, scans, screenshots and defects fixed."
         CanonicalPath="/evidence" />
<PageIntro Eyebrow="Evidence · Development Proof"
           Title="The product should be judged by what can be inspected."
           Summary="Current capability, historical milestones and planned work are labelled separately. Public proof uses fictional or sanitized records." />
<section class="proof-strip standalone">
  <div class="page-shell proof-grid">
    @foreach (var metric in PublicContent.ProofMetrics)
    {
      <article><strong>@metric.Value</strong><span>@metric.Label</span><small>@metric.Detail</small></article>
    }
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-shell section">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Release map</p><h2>Current, historical and planned are not interchangeable.</h2></div>
  <div class="milestone-grid">
    <article><StatusBadge Text="CURRENT" Kind="success" /><h3>LifeOS v26 private beta</h3><p>Website packaging, onboarding, factual case study and public-boundary validation through Group 116.</p><a href="/case-study">Case study →</a></article>
    <article><StatusBadge Text="COMPLETE" Kind="success" /><h3>Desktop and Full Mobile</h3><p>Separate purpose-built products aligned through Group 116 with review-first and offline-safe boundaries.</p><a href="/product">Product overview →</a></article>
    <article><StatusBadge Text="HISTORICAL" Kind="neutral" /><h3>Companion v0.1 beta</h3><p>Lightweight capture, glance, review, outbox and send-to-desktop application.</p><a href="/docs/modules/mobile-companion">Companion module →</a></article>
    <article><StatusBadge Text="NEXT" Kind="warning" /><h3>v27 Release Candidate</h3><p>Final cross-product validation and explicit owner approval remain required.</p><a href="/roadmap">Roadmap →</a></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-shell section">
  <div class="evidence-columns">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">Repository proof</p><h2>Release gates</h2><ul class="check-list"><li>Release builds and automated tests</li><li>Static Website publish output</li><li>Vulnerability and secret scans</li><li>Broken-link and public-output checks</li><li>Clean origin synchronization</li></ul></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">Public proof boundary</p><h2>Inspectable without leaking private state</h2><ul class="check-list"><li>Approved fictional or sanitized identities</li><li>No client data or local records</li><li>No local endpoints, machine names or raw logs</li><li>No secrets, tokens or waitlist submissions</li><li>No installers or binaries in Website assets</li></ul></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="page-shell section">
  <SafetyCallout Label="Evidence boundary"
                 Title="Proof supports a claim; it does not erase product limits."
                 Text="Screenshots, tests and release records demonstrate reviewed behavior. They do not turn planned work into available capability or expose private records." />
</section>
